    "spec": "The sheet gains a setting, period numbering from (a date; blank means off; SETTING_CHANGED\nkey=period-numbering-from value=<date>). While the setting is a date and the sheet's today is on\nor after it, a claim opened receives a number within its period: <period name>-<n>, counting from 1\nin each period, and a claim in no period is numbered X-<n> in its own sequence. Claims opened\nbefore that keep their sheet-wide numbers, and the sheet-wide sequence continues if the setting\nis cleared.\n",
    "prompt": "You are implementing ONE change to this application.\n\nFIRST read AGENTS.md \u2014 it states the working rules and how the app is tested, and sends you to\nDESIGN.md for the app's stack and conventions. Follow both.\n\nTHE CHANGE REQUEST:\nThe sheet gains a setting, period numbering from (a date; blank means off; SETTING_CHANGED\nkey=period-numbering-from value=<date>). While the setting is a date and the sheet's today is on\nor after it, a claim opened receives a number within its period: <period name>-<n>, counting from 1\nin each period, and a claim in no period is numbered X-<n> in its own sequence. Claims opened\nbefore that keep their sheet-wide numbers, and the sheet-wide sequence continues if the setting\nis cleared.\n\nYour work is verified by an automated Playwright UI test already installed under e2e/specs/.\nRead that spec: it declares the exact data-testid anchors, values, test data and any audit\nrecords it expects \u2014 match them. Run `bin/e2e` to build the app, start it, and run the test as\nyou work; iterate until it passes. Change whatever the request needs across the app \u2014 its stored\ndata, its server and its front end. Do NOT edit bin/build, bin/start, bin/stop, bin/e2e,\nAGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, DESIGN.md, e2e/support/ or the test spec.\n"
